{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why","id":1411232,"title":"Favorite Clans and Why","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-31T10:59:22-07:00","id":1411232,"title":"Favorite Clans and Why","content":"In this thread discuss your favorite clan. I'll start:<br /> <br /> Venture- I used to not like or necessarily dislike them at first. At the time I felt they were just too vanilla compared to the other interesting clans, but over time they became my favorite from the sheer awesomeness they were in the Dark Ages, shadow rulers of Rome in Antiquity and how their practically the de facto rulers of Vampire society if either Camarilla, Anarch, or Sabbat. I as a per their clan, they have baseline access to the two most potent disciplines for manipulating the Kine and other Kindred to their whims: Dominate and Presence; on top of which they also possess Fortitude which already makes them more OP if they ever scramble with a Hunter or just general fight.<br /> <br /> Nagaraja- My first real favorite clan as I kept reading VTM material. The whole aspect of them having to eat flesh on top of having to consume blood as usual is a really cool, but also challenging trait about them. The Nagaraja also can eat the corpus of Wraiths and drain their Pathos as a substitute for blood, which is the reason they can have bases in the Underworld. They also have a very interesting name that relates to an obscure part of South Asian mythology. <br /> <br /> Tzimisce- Hands down one of the best of VTM, the Lords of the Land and the riveters of Flesh itself. Each Tzimisce can either be a bloodthirsty warrior, a scholar trying to better understand the facets of immortality, or just plain freaks who'd like nothing more than to craft up unique and crazy abominations every night. This clan lets do the more creative things with the craziness of Vicissitude and its also a bonus to bare Animalism with it because you can easily gather up a bunch of wildlife to create your own strange creatures. Beyond that, the Tzimisce are interesting because despite their solitary nature, even among their own other clan mates, they throughout Kindred history have been in embroiled in very interesting conspiracies. My general favorite parts about them is when their Antediluvian, the Eldest, made other branches in Central America and West Africa- especially athe Naglopers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T11:34:31-07:00","id":1411233,"title":"","content":"There are no bad clans.(But there are some terrible bloodlines). I feel Toreador are the least rewarding because they're neither particularly good or bad at anything and don't want for much, but I kind of enjoy hating them for that? <br /> Auspex, Dominate and Obfuscate are the best disciplines to play with... but Malkavian culture is kinda weak insofar as a malkavians don't really follow an archtype (their often players do, but that's not really something we should consider) <br /> The Trinity of good culture are the Nosferatu, Ventrue and Tremere. They also have rocking disciplines and rocking weaknesses and they encourage players to play smart. The Malkavians, Toreador and Gangrel can just cut their losses and run when things go bad but the good trinity are forced to play real smart, but there's more diversity options than the independent and sabbat clans which you often can't justify playing in Camarilla games. <br /> <br /> But I also like Brujah for dumb fun so... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T12:14:41-07:00","id":1411235,"title":"","content":"Assamites - silent killers, middle eastern ninjas combined with one of the coolest arts in the 2nd edition Player Guide, was one of the coolest things during the early years of playing at teen ages, with time and reading he became wise judges , ambassadors in addition to spies as the game matured to the gaming group.<br /> <br /> Tremere - powerful wizards capable of almost anything in the game, funny how in the beginning the clans gained different nuances, usurper survivors who should not even consider themselves as a clan, I love the hierarchy, dominance and structure that allowed the priramide to survive for so long against so many enemies during history.<br /> <br /> Gangrel - became my favorite clan recently, wanderers, gypsies, outlaws, living in freedom night after night, the concept of the strange and mysterious wanderer able to adapt and survive in addition to protecting himself and protecting others if necessary without relying on money, servants, influences or tricks ,.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T14:08:29-07:00","id":1411247,"title":"","content":"My favorite clan is Toreador. I just love them for their versatility. They have combat ability with celerity, they have investigation and sensory powers with Auspex, and they also have social powers with Presence. On top of that, they don't have any real, solid Archetype or strict clan structure to adhere to, so it's not like being a Tremere or a Ventrue where you just 'have' to be a blood mage or a buisinessman or somesuch. And unlike those nasty Brujah they don't have any negative sterotypes beyond being viewed as flighty or slightly weak (an illusion that is easily dispelled with the proper application of Celerity.)<br /> <br /> They also don't have any of those crippling weaknesses that force them to live in certain ways just to survive. Like Ventrue who need to be rich or influential so they can get their special blood, or Nosferatu who need to live in the shadows because of their ugliness. A Toreador is as equally at home on the street, or in the boardroom, or anywhere else one could think of. Except outside in the afternoon sun, that is.<br /> <br /> A Toreador can be whatever they want to be, experience whatever they want to experience and on top of that they also fit in just about anywhere, Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarch, whatever. Just as Akriel intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","user":"NuclearSnake","date":". 08-31-2020, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T14:13:21-07:00","id":1411250,"title":"","content":"My top trio are the Lasombra, because their theme as &quot;masters in the dark&quot;, thei shadow powers and their connection to the sea are all things which I find cool, Ravnos, because I really love tricksters and illusionists, and the Salubri, because they are both noble, tragic and tainted all in the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T18:38:56-07:00","id":1411284,"title":"","content":"I love the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T21:23:16-07:00","id":1411298,"title":"","content":"Most of the clans are pretty cool, but I have a loathing for any and all that are strongly associated with any form of blood magic. <br /> <br /> Magic spell systems have the same problem in any RPG. Over the course of any given edition of any given fantasy game line, there will inevitably be books sold separately that contribute to nothing but power creep for the spellcasters.<br /> <br /> We hates it forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T00:17:14-07:00","id":1411302,"title":"","content":"It's an explicitly supernatural game, of course there is going to be magic... what do you honestly expect? Even the basic disciplines all the Clans utilize technically count as &quot;magic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T02:22:14-07:00","id":1411311,"title":"","content":"Ravnos: rogues, tricksters, karmic killers, what's not to love. unfortunately, I don't get to play them much, cause I suck. their clan weakness could use a rework<br /> <br /> Brujah: not a fan of the rebels, I'm more into the debaters and devil's advocates types. their discipline spread works, but hard to play cause of their weakness<br /> <br /> Toreador antitribu: the revised version (don't like the 2e version much).<br /> individualists in the sect of vinculum, human clan in the sect of inhumans. irredeemably depraved and parasitic, even among the sabbat since they suck with their rather weak discipline spread,<br /> they represent everything wrong about the sabbat and vampires in general, and I love it.<br /> my only issue with them is that their parasitic nature is a necessity, not just a choice,<br /> they depend way too much on the vinculum and other sabbat social structures to keep the others on board with them,<br /> they can't rely on their powers<br /> <br /> Lasombra: the mary sues of VtM. I don't like them as much as I can't hate them. they're good in every way, they suck at nothing.<br /> best discipline spread, best weakness, fun blood magic (before it got turned into a standard blood magic system similar to thaumaturgy),<br /> they're versatile, they can be anything. fun clan politics.<br /> they're just good, and they get to be tragic about it, because they can't take selfies and admire their marysue-ness in the mirror...so tragic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T03:10:09-07:00","id":1411316,"title":"","content":"As character to play? XD All clans have their unique things about them thatmake them enjoyable to play and great for storytelling. The weaknesses of some are kinda useless (say Toreador) and if you keep in mind that you can learn out of clan disciplines i woulnt focus on disciplines too much when choosing a character. Each clan comes with a special flavour and culture attached to it and has certain &quot;standards&quot; - now vampires are all about individualism and narcisism so being different is a thing, but the general clan will still have some flair to it.<br /> <br /> That said, some clans are way more powerfull than others because of their in clan disciplines and culture. I think Tremere take the cake for thaumaturgy alone. Its by far the most versatile and powerfull discipline.<br /> A close second for me is old clan Tzimisce cause coldunic sorcery and the warform are absolute killers, in special as sorcery doesnt require bloodpoints to be spent.<br /> Third for me would be Nosferatu. Use animalism to create a decoy, sneak up with obfuscate, strike with potence. Killer combo.<br /> Though in open combat the Brujah with celerity and potence own everyone else.<br /> <br /> If we talk high level then its absolutely Azaneali. Shadow form from Obtenebration combined with fire immunity from Daimonion? You are only vulnerable by magic (and who has that but the Tremere and mages) or sunlight. Talk godmode. And if that wasnt enough you get to play with shadow attacks AND Hellfire to anihilate your opponents. Not to mention they also have acces to thaumaturgy, Dur an Ki and Koldunic sorcery through pacts.<br /> <br /> Flairwise though my absolute favorite are the Baali. Nothing beats the double masquerade and infernalism. The secrecy, the slow corruption of fellow characters, the darkness...marvellous. Secret meetings with the coven, playing in the Tal Mahe Ra? Just fckn wow. Their neonates get exposed to territory that most elders dont dable into. Also their embrace is very unique too. Or you join later with apostacy ^^<br /> <br /> Second are the Tremere. Clan Tremere has a very unique culture to it, very close knit group and magical atmosphere.<br /> <br /> Third...i actually like Toreador. They are masters at being puppeteers ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 09-01-2020, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T06:25:48-07:00","id":1411337,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce would be my personal favorite. They are selfish, arrogant, territorial and vain, but they generally keep their word and have a way with animals. <br /> <br /> I would fit right in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T08:06:19-07:00","id":1411353,"title":"","content":"Ventrue, first clan I ever played. The discipline spread is great, especially since we play with DA:V20 rules which gives Fortitude a bump. And if you play them right, you don't have to be a typical business person.<br /> <br /> Lasombra, who doesn't love a Master of Shadows. Almost as good as Ventrue in Manipulation but can punch you into oblivion.<br /> <br /> Assamite but only the DA version with viziers, I found the assassin as sole angle a little boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T08:48:55-07:00","id":1411358,"title":"","content":"I think some clans are misunderstood here. <br /> -Toreador weakness is supposed to occur far more often than most storytellers play it as. It's also an exploitable weakness; Just hang a bauble from the barrel of your shotgun and you've killed yourself a Toreador. <br /> - Thaumaturgy RAI/RAW isn't that powerful and is a huge drain on XP and resources (time spent studying is time not spent doing other things; It's usually smarter to have more retainers or resources or closer connections or something like that than an extra spell), plus it's entirely useless in a frenzy. <br /> -Most Lasombra are clowns, they play second fiddle to the Ventrue for a reason. I like the arrogance, I like the demands of excellence, but most of them are bullies posturing with delusions of grandeur. That makes them really fun to play. If you can manage to achieve the mary-sue status as a lasombra, you could probably do it with any clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T09:45:04-07:00","id":1411361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411358#post1411358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Most Lasombra are clowns, they play second fiddle to the Ventrue for a reason. I like the arrogance, I like the demands of excellence, but most of them are bullies posturing with delusions of grandeur. That makes them really fun to play. If you can manage to achieve the mary-sue status as a lasombra, you could probably do it with any clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>sir mary sue says: &quot;you're absolutely right&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://store-images.s-microsoft.com/image/apps.5637.65749786814923168.a6bc7691-4449-44ac-a7cd-18b5195a3439.a2cb0461-3b8d-4392-9249-69c5f5711929?mode=scale&amp;q=90&amp;h=1080&amp;w=1920\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T09:53:43-07:00","id":1411365,"title":"","content":"My favorite are probably the Tremere, though I like a lot of the Clans. The Tremere are my favorite not for the reason most may think, it's not Thaumaturgy. I like the Tremere because of the themes and flavor of the Clan. I like the organization. They are a secret society that is very hierarchical, they have all kinds of rituals and secret societies within their already secret society. They are utterly ruthless in their pursuit of knowledge and power. They clawed their way into vampiric society despite the odds against them. They take being a vampire seriously. I actually think I would like them as much if they didn't have Thaumaturgy, though such a change would require a little reworking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:49:57-07:00","id":1411381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411365#post1411365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite are probably the Tremere, though I like a lot of the Clans. The Tremere are my favorite not for the reason most may think, it's not Thaumaturgy. I like the Tremere because of the themes and flavor of the Clan. I like the organization. They are a secret society that is very hierarchical, they have all kinds of rituals and secret societies within their already secret society. They are utterly ruthless in their pursuit of knowledge and power. They clawed their way into vampiric society despite the odds against them. They take being a vampire seriously. I actually think I would like them as much if they didn't have Thaumaturgy, though such a change would require a little reworking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have to hand it to the Tremere as a clan concept; as you say, these guys sat down, thought about it really hard, did the homework, and then sought out the vampiric condition. That's pretty gangsta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T11:56:47-07:00","id":1411398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411381#post1411381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do have to hand it to the Tremere as a clan concept; as you say, these guys sat down, thought about it really hard, did the homework, and then sought out the vampiric condition. That's pretty gangsta.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Though if I were writing the backstory and metaplot myself, I would have dramatically reduced the number of enemies that the Tremere took on at once. Just fighting against the Tzimisce was enough of a feat. But they also went to war with the Gangrel and Nosferatu, because they created Gargoyles which then revolted and had to be fought. They had to fight the Order of Hermes too and during all of this they are exterminating the Salubri. They helped fight the Anarchs and cemented a position in the Camarilla for themselves. Then there is the curse with the Assamites. The more enemies you add in there, the sillier it gets. I would streamline that backstory a bit, take away some of the enemies, and I think it would be a bit more reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T12:05:26-07:00","id":1411402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411361#post1411361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> sir mary sue says: &quot;you're absolutely right&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://store-images.s-microsoft.com/image/apps.5637.65749786814923168.a6bc7691-4449-44ac-a7cd-18b5195a3439.a2cb0461-3b8d-4392-9249-69c5f5711929?mode=scale&amp;q=90&amp;h=1080&amp;w=1920\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, is that Jackie Estacado? I always thought he would make for a good lasombra...aside for the whole Jenny thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T12:14:17-07:00","id":1411403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuclearSnake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411402#post1411402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, is that Jackie Estacado? I always thought he would make for a good lasombra...aside for the whole Jenny thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>the Jenny thing can work for a Lasombra antitribu (camarilla or independant),<br /> he could also work as a king of shadow (humanist lasombra in the sabbat)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T12:15:35-07:00","id":1411404,"title":"","content":"I love them all, no matter that more than a few of them are superfluous.<br /> <br /> My personal favorites at the moment:<ul><li><b>The Ravnos</b> - specifically, the post-Revised version seen in Dark Ages' Thieves in the Night and the revised Ravnos clanbook. They're an interesting collection of diverse subcultures united by an unwanted compulsion for sin and a Beast that is perhaps more insidious and clever than that of other clans.</li> <li><b>The Assamites</b> - again, the post-Revised version in Wolves at the Door and the revised Assamite clanbook. Especially the Vizier/Scholar caste, but I enjoy all three. I can relate to their tendency toward monomania and enjoy their overall versatility and general questing for some sort of higher truth.</li> <li><b>The Nosferatu</b> - I've always had a soft spot for outcasts and tragic monsters, and I like how they usually manage to carry themselves with a sense of dignity in spite of their curse.</li> <li><b>The Ventrue</b> - Once I actually got my head around them and their whole noblesse oblige + obsession with dignity thing, they became one of my favorites.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T12:17:17-07:00","id":1411405,"title":"","content":"They didn't really 'Take on all the enemies at once'; they weren't playing horde mode or anything like that. <br /> <br /> <br /> At the turn of the millenium, Clan Tremere was founded. The Tzmisce who are almost entirely uninterested in that which occurs outside of their personal domains. The Tremere still had plenty of mortal mages and human servants with them at this point. <br /> A hundred years later, Some Gangrel and Nosferatu who knew what was going on once the Tremere had created their minmaxed murder-servants. Saulot was diablerised ten years after. The Salubri were hunted down (but, y'know, they were never a powerful clan, especially considering most of them are pacifistic) <br /> Another hundred years later (and after the Tremere were accepted at many courts), the hermetics realised what had happened (They didn't really have any motivations to look into all this) and warred with the Tremere for a couple of decades. Oh, and they had Baali help. I wonder for how long? <br /> <br /> &quot;The omen war&quot; is really a series of sporadic skirmishes and minor campaigns. It wasn't an apocalyptic tooth and nail fight for the clan's survival, though it is really cool to imagine Gargoyle/Horrid form Dogfights above the carpathians. It sounds really impressive, and the Tremere almost certainly talk big about it. But it was hardly worse than modern sectarian conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T12:31:37-07:00","id":1411409,"title":"","content":"There isn't any clan I dislike and I like each of them for various reasons but my favorite with a couple honorable mentions.<br /> <br /> Gangrel have always been my favorite clan. I like any game or character archetype that leans into the animalistic side of the human nature. They're also just a very versatile clan where their main personality trait is simply a heightened sense of the will to survive and overcome hardship. I love that I can choose almost any character concept and find an interesting spin with the Gangrel. Their disciplines seem very one note on first glance but I've found great uses for animalism and form of mist is probably their best power overall. Such a good clan.<br /> <br /> Next would probably be the Nosferatu because as a teenager the visuals of them really sparked my imagination and just made VTM something totally different than any other RPG id played up to that point. Their culture and outlook was very interesting to read into and I'd always have a powerful warren of Nossies in my campaigns to get into everything and cause chaos.<br /> <br /> Finally Im a huge fan of the Sabbat and the Tzimisce are the reason why. Their history and how it shaped their clan and then how that in turn shaped the formation of the Sabbat and everything to come after was something that again as a teenager really ignited my imagination and I have a lot of fond memories of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T12:32:04-07:00","id":1411410,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> we all know who's the best Lasombra:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://steamuserimages-a.akamaihd.net/ugc/812181709688246532/DDA53BA5BC93A63D95073B6D7C81319B0D4B99A2/\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T13:33:29-07:00","id":1411428,"title":"","content":"I'll be the odd one and say I've had some of the most fun playing Followers of Set and just being a manipulative bastard and using people as weapons through trickery and deception. You've also got elements of Gnosticism, which I find to be a fascinating world view.<br /> <br /> I do dig the Tremere, I mean come on, blood magic is awesome. Then they've got their whole Illuminati Pyramid scheme going on, too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T14:50:15-07:00","id":1411435,"title":"","content":"I find it difficult to explain in detail, but I especially like Giovanni because they're so <i>lurid</i>. Somehow, vampire infernalists crosses a line for me, whereas a network of vampire, necromancer, merchant aristocrats and their associates doesn't. The opulence, depravity and power tripping are themes of the Camarilla, but the Giovanni embody them more crudely. And as a bonus, their business crosses over with <i>Wraith</i>. I think I'd still appreciate them if they had nothing much to do with vampires, but I barely question why there should be vampire necromancers and not vampires who turn into snakes or vampire tricksters with illusion powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T14:59:34-07:00","id":1411437,"title":"","content":"Ventrue, Toreador, Tzimisce, Setites, Tremere, Lasombra antitribu<br /> <br /> Other than the Tremere (who I like cause they\u2019re wizards) and the Tzimisce (because of the whole Romantic Dracula thing), these are all very social clans. I like playing characters like that. I don\u2019t hate any of the clans, and I even like the Nosferatu in V5 now that they\u2019re more like subtly creepy and less blatantly hideous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T15:19:06-07:00","id":1411441,"title":"","content":"They're still hideous, it's just the clan art is bad. Subtly creepy nosferatu is a requiem thing.<br /> <br /> Also the Nos weakness of ugly forces clan unity and smart plays. Alas, I can't bring myself to play Nos in V5 because the third level obfuscate power, appearing as anyone you can think of, so crucial to many playstyles, is now a 5th level power. I don't wanna be a hundred years old to put up convincing alter-egos. Also Potence took a significant hit in V5 and so my brilliant-totally original trademark nosferatu fighting style (GRAB AND BITE) doesn't work so well. I can't swim or dig so well. Fortunately I can go all-in on animalism and the difference isn't that big.<br /> <br /> Actually, if we go by V5, the best clans are:<br /> Gangrel: Would never have picked these guys for best clan in the normal game, but they're the least harmed by discipline changes. Presence is stronger too, but clans with presence took other hits (it's paired with obfuscate, auspex or dominate... all took hefty hits), so I like Gangrel best. Maybe Ravnos will benefit. So far we have Gangrel, country gangrel and fish-boy gangrel most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T06:12:20-07:00","id":1411498,"title":"","content":"In that case, I take it back. I like Requiem Nosferatu, not V5 Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T09:41:46-07:00","id":1411517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411441#post1411441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also the Nos weakness of ugly forces clan unity and smart plays.</div> </div> </div> </div>imo, we already have enough insentives for that without having to add more restrictive clan curses,<br /> we can easily replace Nosferatu with vampire oucats and hackers digging tunnels or living in the sewers to escape the tyranny of the sects or some such (which is what I think they're trying to do by nuking shrecknet and making anarchs into riggers),<br /> and we have yet to solve other issues like night vision, technology, short nights in certain areas and discipline use that doesn't result in overfeeding and mass murder etc before we have to think about clan specific restrictions,<br /> <br /> &quot;smart play&quot; isn't that appealing, we already have our hands full with feeding management, masquerade and the beast,<br /> the night is too short to squeeze in more Vampire: the Logistics into it,<br /> leave some space for drama and some bloody fun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T10:33:51-07:00","id":1411524,"title":"","content":"I like the Nosferatu, their Clan weakness, and the Clan culture that it creates. As with any Clan, but more so in their case, you shouldn't get too hung up in logistics if you want a game focused on something else. If your V:tM chronicle is focused on the intrigues between elders while the Sabbat is trying to infiltrate the city, then you don't want to spend a lot of time trying to find victims, drink blood, clean up the mess, avoid cell phone cameras, and so on. It would be nice, though, if Obfuscate carried over for pictures and video since these days cameras are everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T11:28:09-07:00","id":1411529,"title":"","content":"<b>Brujah.</b> The long, slow fall from philosopher-kings to rabble, the passion and the rage. The history and sense of old crimes back at the start of the bronze age. How some of them have causes that they throw themselves into, the 70s communists, and older causes, getting passionate about dead issues. Know-nothings, abolitionists, Anti-Masonists. How most of them don't have any particular case. The most varied clan, supporting so many concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T12:26:49-07:00","id":1411535,"title":"","content":"When I said 'smart plays' I meant acting sick, wearing fabulous costume makeup, rugging up, playing a full-time ninja, Animalism 3'ing everyone who sees you, obfuscating everywhere if you're not feeling particularly creative, developing a number of different personas and fooling everyone into thinking you're multiple people...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411517#post1411517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">imo, we already have enough insentives for that without having to add more restrictive clan curses,</div> </div> </div> </div> what does that even mean? I'm not saying 'make the Nos more bad'. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> we can easily replace Nosferatu with vampire oucats and hackers digging tunnels or living in the sewers to escape the tyranny of the sects or some such (which is what I think they're trying to do by nuking shrecknet and making anarchs into riggers), </div> </div> </div> That's dumb. Why would we do that? Get rid of a cool clan so we can have more useless anarchs with a fondness of utilities? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and we have yet to solve other issues like night vision, technology, short nights in certain areas and discipline use that doesn't result in overfeeding and mass murder etc before we have to think about clan specific restrictions, </div> </div> </div> If you're not playing the latest edition, most of this is easy. For the stuff that isn't fixed by not playing V5: Vampires don't hang round the poles during summer, night vision isn't a problem (though sewers are dark enough to be a problem, nos can get around this through memory, tactile senses, and learning the first dot of either auspex or protean, or using a light in modern nights)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;smart play&quot; isn't that appealing, we already have our hands full with feeding management, masquerade and the beast, </div> </div> </div> All this should be pretty intuitive. Now, If you wanna play mental tertiaries, you're welcome to it, but don't try to screw it for people who want more than that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the night is too short to squeeze in more Vampire: the Logistics into it,<br /> leave some space for drama and some bloody fun </div> </div> </div> Am I getting strawmanned here or what? Even so, a lot of people enjoy meticulous planning or finding creative solutions to problems. Strategy games aren't as big as arcade shooters but that doesn't mean the latter is objectively better than the former. Vampire's strength is that it can acomadate all kinds of play (though some will let you live longer than others) .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-02-2020, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T12:54:27-07:00","id":1411539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411535#post1411535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what does that even mean? I'm not saying 'make the Nos more bad'.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, I'm saying their clan weakness is already too bad,<br /> standard nosferatu that look like monsters but still have symmetrical faces and distinguishable features is ok,<br /> but when half the Nos are twisted all over with weird puss bubbles or a beak instead of a mouth and have to feed on mosquitos and humans' eyeballs (canon btw)...that goes a bit too far imo<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's dumb. Why would we do that? Get rid of a cool clan so we can have more useless anarchs with a fondness of utilities? </div> </div> </div>no, I was saying Nosferatu don't need those specific clan features to justify their habits (though, I admit, I don't find them cool at all, for the reasons I mentioned above...yes, I'm shallow that way)<br /> <br /> as for the devs trying to replace/change the nosferatu, I just get that feeling from the latest edition,<br /> maybe they just want to give the anarchs some of the nosferatu's stuff, like they did when they gave them blood magic,<br /> but that's a matter for another thread<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I getting strawmanned here or what? </div> </div> </div>if that's the case, it wasn't my intention,<br /> <br /> I simply infered from your posts on topics concerning Necromancers, Tremere and Ventrue that you were into management games (which I like too, but not in VtM) and seemed to favor clans that had to play the management game the most,<br /> and I assumed (wrongly I guess) that's what you meant by &quot;smart play&quot; in your previous posts,<br /> <br /> anyway, sorry for the lack of clarity in my post, I lack eloquence<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T13:08:42-07:00","id":1411542,"title":"","content":"Lasombra for sure. Powers of this Abyss combined with a cutthroat success at all costs darwinism mentality makes for a fun clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T13:52:48-07:00","id":1411554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411539#post1411539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no, I'm saying their clan weakness is already too bad,<br /> standard nosferatu that look like monsters but still have symmetrical faces and distinguishable features is ok,<br /> but when half the Nos are twisted all over with weird puss bubbles or a beak instead of a mouth and have to feed on mosquitos and humans' eyeballs (canon btw)...that goes a bit too far imo</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I feel like nosferatu (and others with the curse of ugly) should have a 'default' ugly and then they should have merits and flaws to influence that.<br /> <br /> Default: You look horrifying. A good look of you makes you inhuman but you could hide features and escape a cursory look. A modern audience would look at you and think some combination of horrid accident, birth defects, medical condition, and extreme body modification. Samedi look like corpses but it's more -oh shit this guy looks like a corpse- rather than -Oh shit this corpse is walking around-.<br /> 3 point merit- You look like a really unfortunate human<br /> 5 point merit- you even look sympathetic<br /> 1 point flaw- Your appearance is either an easy masquerade breach (but you look like an indeterminate monster), or you specifically have vampire features.<br /> 1 point flaw- You give off the impression that you are diseased and contagious.<br /> 3 point flaw- You're a horrific monster that makes even your bloodline recoil in horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if that's the case, it wasn't my intention,<br /> <br /> I simply infered from your posts on topics concerning Necromancers, Tremere and Ventrue that you were into management games (which I like too, but not in VtM) and seemed to favor clans that had to play the management game the most, </div> </div> </div>I posted my favourite clans here. The Corpse fuckers are so-so and I've never played one (if I did, i'd play a Samedi hands down and they don't even have it in clan.) The Tremere are a multi-faceted clan with a lot of variation in what you can do (so long as you serve the pyramid) . The main distinct playstyles that come to mind are that you can play a manager, you can play someone who doesn't give a fuck about politics and just wants to wizard, and you can play gestapo. All three of these are fun, and you can of course combine all three of them into the most typical tremere you can. You could also play against type somewhat and be the face of the clan. The Ventrue... yeah, ok, there's a bit less versatility, but it's mostly the same: you can play the accountant, the CEO, the firebrand priest, the crusader... You can manage your money intimately and write up a list or you can go with 'Storyteller, I have 4 resources so can we say I have a helicopter'. You can manage your servvants and ghouls and private army and mob and herd or you can just say &quot;I send in some guys to deal with it&quot; (Honestly, you do need a little bit of a discussion with your GM even when you're minimalistic about this sorta thing) or as a Ventrue you can just dominate some people on the fly or prep a dominate for a plan or...<br /> <br /> You can totally have an empire in game but not-get-into-it if it bogs you down. 'I have 4 dots of X' works if you want to keep things simple. I do like getting meticulous about things, but to me the best way of doing that is giving the storyteller a piece of paper with some important things and a simple overview of what my character owns/runs in the background and saying 'you got a problem with any of this?' That way you can keep this stuff out of the way of the game until it's necessary. You can handwave a lot of background stuff in vampire if you don't want to delve into it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like I've said before; I still appreciate playing a brujah and just punching things. I can literally play any kind of character. Nosferatu are a clan I like because they can be incredibly minimalist or very involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T22:47:05-07:00","id":1411607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411554#post1411554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I feel like nosferatu (and others with the curse of ugly) should have a 'default' ugly and then they should have merits and flaws to influence that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I make something similar , in my games all vampires start getting deformities/supernatural traits called marks of the beast when their path rating is very low (3-) and this gives penalties to social interactions with humans and seduction if discovered (wich may be a masquerade breach).<br /> <br /> However in the case of Nos they start wich one mark of the beast that never goes away , devolop other marks of the beast quickier and cannot spend willpower in social interactions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T23:09:54-07:00","id":1411609,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve sometimes thought it might be interesting to change the Gangrel flaw so that they become more bestial as their Humanity score gets lower rather than gaining a feature based on frenzies. It might have the unintended consequence of making Gangrel highly moral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T23:40:41-07:00","id":1411611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411539#post1411539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but when half the Nos are twisted all over with weird puss bubbles or a beak instead of a mouth and have to feed on mosquitos and humans' eyeballs (canon btw)...that goes a bit too far imo</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. The clan exists because the game designers wanted to be sure there could be PCs that looked like Count Orlock from the original Nosferatu movie (which was a good choice since its iconic). Rather than keeping them just bizarre, they made them a little more monstrous, but that was OK. Josh Timbrook's art was a great selling point in the first days of the game, and his Nosferatu were a nice combination of the grotesque, sinister, and uncanny. But it didn't take long before the game kept making them more and more disgusting. <br /> <br /> I don't mind there being some variation from the classic Orlock look (I think Nosferatu should be able to fill any of the rolls of monstrous blood eaters of the night from Black Annis to Grendel), but I think they went overboard. Probably because of an overemphasis that the Nosferatu were people who hung out in the sewers which augmented the disgust factor.<br /> <br /> I do think MyWifeIsScary has a good point of allowing Merits/Flaws to adjust the extent of their appearance.<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with the V5 rules so I don't know how that has impacted them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T07:46:30-07:00","id":1411641,"title":"","content":"My favorite has changed as I have gotten older. Back in the day with 1e I was all about the Malkavians (I was also in middle school so...you know).<br /> For most of my time playing 2e and Revised I was a big Tremere and Tzimisce fan. I really enjoyed the hermetic mode of the Tremere, and I loved the idea of being able to remake yourself like the Tzimisce.<br /> Now as I have aged up, I find myself more and more liking the Toreador. They can fit in anywhere, have a great range of starting disciplines, and just seem so much more flexible and quietly powerful than others. They love art and culture, and don't seem to feel the need in general to flex all the time like the Lasombra or Ventrue.<br /> I guess being a Toreador just seems a little less restrictive than most of the other clans. I kind of feel the same way about the Brujah too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T11:27:09-07:00","id":1411658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411609#post1411609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve sometimes thought it might be interesting to change the Gangrel flaw so that they become more bestial as their Humanity score gets lower rather than gaining a feature based on frenzies. It might have the unintended consequence of making Gangrel highly moral.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a genuinely great idea. Any number of clan weaknesses could be houseruled to get worse as one's score drops, and it would really heighten the nightmare of low Humanity.<br /> <br /> A full development of the idea might be a solid idea for any Storyteller's Vault authors reading this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:32:34-07:00","id":1411672,"title":"","content":"Clan Toreador, of course. What's a better way to spend eternity than to delve into culture and refinement? <br /> <br /> Also Clan Lasombra, for their exploration of the darker parts of unlife. I especially like the pre-Embrace testing to destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T14:11:46-07:00","id":1411694,"title":"","content":"I heard there was a Nosferatu in Montreal by Night who lived underwater and was basically a literal sea monster. I also heard there are Gangrel who live underwater too, but that might be Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T14:53:26-07:00","id":1411705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411694#post1411694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard there was a Nosferatu in Montreal by Night who lived underwater and was basically a literal sea monster. I also heard there are Gangrel who live underwater too, but that might be Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are a fair number of aquatic Nossies and a bloodline of Gangrel called Mariners in VtM, or at least there used to be. Not sure if they still exist after V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T15:50:16-07:00","id":1411711,"title":"","content":"Here's my preferences. Note that they are built on the clan's culture and not on its mechanics (which would be just disciplines and clan flaw after all).<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah</b>: because I like how they play against the classical stereotype of the vampire incarnated by the Ventrue. Brujah dream... and they rage against those who would stop them from acheiving it. I also like the duality within the clan, philosopher kings, warrior scholars, rebels with a cause, fighters for justice that always risk becoming what they swear to destroy because of their fury.<br /> <br /> <b>Assamite</b>: back in the old days, when I was young and stupid and the clan was introduced I thought the Assamites were the good guys. After all they hunted down other vampires who abused humanity. It took me a while to realize that was a naive reading of the Assamites. Fortunately revised came along (and libellus sanguinis 3 as well) and with it came one of the best (if not the best) clanbook of them all... and it was clanbook Assamite. Rather than staying as a generic blood cult of assassins the clan gained much depth and a fascinating history populated with incredible figures. Because of their nature Assamites were never easy to play in normal VtM games but to this day I find them one of the most rewarding clans to play and to include in any chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b>: like the Ventrue but better. These guys want results and are willing to do whatever it takes to get them. It's impossible to talk about them without mentioning their shadow-mastery but that's not all they are. They can be surprisingly human (back in DA I dare say they were one of the most humane clans) or the most wicked of monsters sometimes because they believe that by becoming monsters they are serving God's plan to make humanity better. All that said, it's very simple, the Lasombra manage to have the good qualities of the Ventrue and add an undeniable cool factor the dull patricians never dreamed of having.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> About the Tremere. Keep in mind House Tremere actually predates Vampire the Masquerade as a game. It can be argued the Tremere influenced and shaped the game in a big way, especially considering how Tremere himself was the favoured character of the guy who invented VtM and used to be the powermongering bad guy even when he was a wizard and the idea of him becoming a vampire had not yet formed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 09-03-2020, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:10:30-07:00","id":1411726,"title":"","content":"Favourite Clans, eh?<br /> <br /> Well, I'll echo some sentiments already expressed by others; it would be easier to list the ones I like less than the rest, to be honest. Let's give it a try, though.<br /> <br /> I have great affection for the Nosferatu, especially falling in love with the Dark Ages clan picture. I love Nosferatu (the movie), Shadow of the Vampire is great fun, I just enjoy this aesthetic, in this game and others. With such a striking Clan Weakness, they're arguably in a position to get a unique discipline... but their spread is already pretty darn perfect! The downside is how the focus seemed to grow more and more towards the icky spectrum rather than monstrous. Granted, some artworks aren't even ugly, but obviously inhuman still.<br /> <br /> On that note, it's silly the glowing vampire eyes are actually a super-rare supernatural flaw and most can't see in the dark. That's worse than Garou keeping human senses in wolf form, since they're at least supposed to spend some time not as a wolf. Vampires are night hunters.<br /> <br /> I also like the Malkavians. Kinda. I like Malkavians who are done well, but fishmalks are, sadly, a thing. I like to think my Malkavians were at least okay, since I never heard any complaints. Only surprise at hearing those actually were Malkavians, now and again. I've come around to sticking with Dominate too. Dementation is, shall we say, a bit situational.<br /> <br /> Being a sucker for Egyptian lore, especially Set, the Followers drew me in too. Even if they're quite miscast. Were I the writer in charge, I'd sprinkle in one or more different origin myths, like hints that their Founder is actually Typhon, not Set, and that the identification with the Egyptian god of foreigners happened after Typhon first visited and sired childer there.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni. Necromancers are great. Necromancer vampire family, with an (un)healthy dose of Bathory sprinkled in? Sign me up! And yes, it does help that they're a very European Clan and that's where most of the chronicles I've played were situated. I wonder if that's the case for others also? It just feels... more right to go with a Giovanni over a Samedi when your game is set in central Europe.<br /> <br /> As noted above, there are also Clans I like less, and those I want to like more than I end up doing.<br /> <br /> I want to like the Tzimisce, but they sometimes strike me as overdone. Plus, they shed the darkly noble aspect almost entirely by modern times, with the freaks now the heart and soul of the Clan. I absolutely LOVE reading about the different lineages in the revised Clanbook, about the Eldest's own childer; in many ways, they feel like the most CLAN of the vampire Clans to me.<br /> <br /> Assamites. Never been a fan of one-note murderfactions. It was a wonderful idea to break them that up a bit.<br /> <br /> Ravnos. They appear to have so much potential, and yet, nobody seems to know what to do with them, so they end up having a bridge dropped on their collective heads. For the Western branch, maybe they could've done something in the manner of a religious movement believing themselves demons possessing dead bodies..? Then have them duke it out with the Lasombra? I'm sure there's SOMETHING that can be done with them.<br /> <br /> And least liked... are some of the bloodlines. Is that cheating?<br /> The Daughters of Cacophony and the Kyasid. The former are kinda just there, and the latter read like someone's self-insert.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:13:46-07:00","id":1411727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411705#post1411705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are a fair number of aquatic Nossies and a bloodline of Gangrel called Mariners in VtM, or at least there used to be. Not sure if they still exist after V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T20:28:51-07:00","id":1411741,"title":"","content":"I've also wanted to play a Kiasyd/Maeghar for awhile, too. Fae blooded vampire that's a 7 foot tall alien, awesome! I really dug the shorty story in Lore of the Bloodlines about Nathaniel McCabe. I know there are technically 2 separate bloodlines there, but either would be fun to play as a creepy bookish nerd. Shame I never get to play these days, I'm pretty much always the one storytelling. I did throw one in as a bartender in Tijuana, but she's been pretty minor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T01:20:32-07:00","id":1411753,"title":"","content":"Kiasyd are really a spit in the face of anyone wanting to play &quot;Vampire, the logistics&quot;*; You can't be a seven foot tall alien looking freak and only rely on Dominate to get you through each night: Mytherceria does not help you feed, Obtenebration... I suppose when you get to 5th level and get some abyss mysticism under your belt you can feed just fine, but that's a problem in itself. A Kiasyd simply can't do night-by night feedings. The only Viable low-level option is to get some ghouls to abduct people for your dungeon, which certainly has it's own significant problems. You can somewhat manage when you can arange one on one meetings and erase the memories from that but even then...<br /> <br /> The only thing that makes the Kiasyd work is the long, long, long period of sire tutelage; because they need 50 years and a lot of money to be viable...<br /> <br /> Two clan-specific disciplines is a pain. I'd make Mytherceria an Auspex &quot;path&quot; to fix that.<br /> For the weakness...<br /> <br /> So the Kiasyd have two. The freak appearance and the weakness to iron. The lesser weakness being the latter.<br /> Iron should work as -soakable with stamina, aggravated damage to heal- rather than -totally unsoakable- , unless we're talking obtenebration (Kiasyd Obtenebration should hate iron) (note: This is my opinion of most aggravated damage in general)<br /> The Freakish appearance... I think what mortals see and what the supernatural see should be different here. Mundane people, kinfolk... they should all see normal people. Ghouls, anything more unatural than ghouls, folks with a good awareness stat... should all see the freak. Now, which form's the true form? Eh. That'd be less of a problem if they weren't so tall. <br /> <br /> Also I think that there should be a wildly held belief that drinking Kiasyd/Maeghar blood should grant you strange powers so people frequently hunt them down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T01:25:11-07:00","id":1411755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411361#post1411361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://store-images.s-microsoft.com/image/apps.5637.65749786814923168.a6bc7691-4449-44ac-a7cd-18b5195a3439.a2cb0461-3b8d-4392-9249-69c5f5711929?mode=scale&amp;q=90&amp;h=1080&amp;w=1920\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a hot picture!<br /> <br /> Anywho, favorite clans. Uh, almost all of them?<br /> <br /> But only certain interpretations of many of them. For instance, I love Vizier-type Assamites, but not actual assassins. I love 'path of the warrior' type Setites more than the drug-dealing corrupters of innocence.<br /> <br /> Tremere and Ventrue and Nosferatu, in general. These three clans, I even like the 'standard' ones, and not just a subset of them.<br /> <br /> I love the *feel* of Lasombra, but kinda hate their disciplines (Obfuscate, Presence and Potence feel like they'd suit their themes better). I love the disciplines of 1st edition Malkavians (with Dominate, I don't like Dementation at all), but there's a very, very fine line on Derangement options that aren't super-annoying. Giovanni powers, so cool, Giovanni themselves, so boringly edgelord. Necrophilia! Titter at faux scandal. (I'd play a Samedi over a Giovanni every day and twice on Sunday, and not even bother with Thanatosis, annoying overspecialized / unnecessary Bloodline Discipline #1823. That said, I love the idea of Necromancy, so, whatever, I'm fine with my own hypocrisy!)<br /> <br /> A weird twist would be for several 'Clans' to actually be mini-Sects, with few or none being Embraced as a Nosferatu, Malkavian, Follower of Set or Assamite, but each being a place where vampires of all sorts of clans end up, some because they are too ugly and nobody else will take them, some too crazy and have nowhere else to go, some because they have been seduced into the worship of Set, and others because they've been enticed into the bloody crusade of Haqim. One might be embraced by someone who was a 'Follower of Set,' but her actual bloodline was Toreador, before she 'saw the dark' and turned to Set's service. But I think everyone would draw the line for what's a clan, and what's one of these sorts of associations / clubs / mini-sects in a different place.<br /> <br /> Even the Tremere could turn out to take in blood sorcerers of all different 'Clans,' and sharing their resources only after the new recruit renounces their ties to their 'birth-Clan' and accepts Tremere as their new 'hermetic father.'<br /> <br /> Or the Lasombra could take their inherent elitism a step beyond, and to becme a Lasombra you must already be a vampire of some other Clan and impress the hell out of the current Les Amies Noir, and they invite you to renounce your birth-Clan (secretly, unlike joining the Tremere, because you are expected to officially remain part of them, and keep your new true loyalties secret!) and join them. But it's a secret. Refusing the invitation is a death-sentence, so few suspect that they do this, or how many of them there are, or who among their own clanmates are secretly Lasombra...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T01:26:07-07:00","id":1411756,"title":"","content":"My in alphabetic order<br /> Salubri: Because they are gentle healers (and protectors during DA) and those are the Roles I love to play in Games.<br /> Tremere: Because it's magic.<br /> True Brujah: Because they incorporate my belief from a true genius. Bleach mayby even albino, stoic and emotionless rational thinker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T21:45:11-07:00","id":1412003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411753#post1411753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiasyd are really a spit in the face of anyone wanting to play &quot;Vampire, the logistics&quot;*; You can't be a seven foot tall alien looking freak and only rely on Dominate to get you through each night: Mytherceria does not help you feed, Obtenebration... I suppose when you get to 5th level and get some abyss mysticism under your belt you can feed just fine, but that's a problem in itself. A Kiasyd simply can't do night-by night feedings. The only Viable low-level option is to get some ghouls to abduct people for your dungeon, which certainly has it's own significant problems. You can somewhat manage when you can arange one on one meetings and erase the memories from that but even then...<br /> <br /> The only thing that makes the Kiasyd work is the long, long, long period of sire tutelage; because they need 50 years and a lot of money to be viable...<br /> <br /> Two clan-specific disciplines is a pain. I'd make Mytherceria an Auspex &quot;path&quot; to fix that.<br /> For the weakness...<br /> <br /> So the Kiasyd have two. The freak appearance and the weakness to iron. The lesser weakness being the latter.<br /> Iron should work as -soakable with stamina, aggravated damage to heal- rather than -totally unsoakable- , unless we're talking obtenebration (Kiasyd Obtenebration should hate iron) (note: This is my opinion of most aggravated damage in general)<br /> The Freakish appearance... I think what mortals see and what the supernatural see should be different here. Mundane people, kinfolk... they should all see normal people. Ghouls, anything more unatural than ghouls, folks with a good awareness stat... should all see the freak. Now, which form's the true form? Eh. That'd be less of a problem if they weren't so tall.<br /> <br /> Also I think that there should be a wildly held belief that drinking Kiasyd/Maeghar blood should grant you strange powers so people frequently hunt them down...</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd work for Mytherceria as an auspex variant, hell one of the powers is almost a dupe of spirit's touch. <br /> <br /> They might not be the best for interacting with mortals, but you can still always put on a hoody, some foundation to cover your skin and sunglasses and you're in better shape than a Nosferatu without mask of a thousand faces trying to deal with humans. It's not the logistics aspect that I'm after if I played that sort of character, but that it would be an interesting roleplaying experience. Other party members can be the face and deal with mortals, you're more the occultist with abyssal mysticism or perhaps necromancy that the group turns to for occult and investigative matters. The character would fill their niche in the party and others can deal with the humans. The medieval version that became the Maeghar also aren't as freakish as the ones that descended from Marconius. You might just have pointed ears, be exceptionally tall, have really hairy legs or something other minor fey influenced appearance trait. That's not to say I don't think logistics are useless, but not every character needs to be good at that provided they can bring something else to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T23:52:34-07:00","id":1412013,"title":"","content":"Every character should be self sufficient in night to night feeding. The Salubri and Capadocians got wiped so easily because their numbers were limited because their disciplines weren't great for feeding. The Nosferatu have three wonderful disciplines to make up for the ugly and the Samedi at least have the best discipline for it. By contrast the Toreador are the successful generalists of the kindred world that have all the powers they need to thrive anywhere civilisation can be found. Kiasyd pose too many challenges.A hoody, sunglasses and dodgy makeup is only going to attract more attention to the guy who look like he had surgery to become an eldari. If they had two dots of obfuscate, It'd be ok, but they don't. Their tranformation is just too extreme for Kiasyd.<br /> <br /> Maeghar... They're not so much of a problem.<br /> <br /> I want my players to play viable characters in a solo session, even if we're in a group. I want players to play believable characters, not something that only exists to fill a niche in the party and has to rely on everyone else for all the normal stuff. A good character shouldn't come from a vacuum to exist only when the party gets together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-05-2020, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T03:37:09-07:00","id":1412041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1411609#post1411609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve sometimes thought it might be interesting to change the Gangrel flaw so that they become more bestial as their Humanity score gets lower rather than gaining a feature based on frenzies. It might have the unintended consequence of making Gangrel highly moral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that unintended consequence would break them as a clan. The thing is, clan weaknesses should push clans into behaving stereotypically. The Ventrue weakness pushes them into wanting peace, order, and changelessness, because they are the clan that most needs their Herd to be safe and stable. The Toreador weakness pushes them towards encouraging art, because their disciplines are strongest when surrounded by beauty. The Brujah weaknesses encourages them to promote chaos, because they are most hidden in places where humans are rioting routinely.<br /> <br /> Making Gangrel suffer especially hard from a low humanity encourages them to behave like old school Salubri. It doesn't fit how they are actually intended to behave. Whereas the animal feature flaw pushes them towards encouraging things to remain rural, since they need to be able to pounce on hitchhickers, campers, and truck-drivers without being caught on camera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T03:56:21-07:00","id":1412044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412041#post1412041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making Gangrel suffer especially hard from a low humanity encourages them to behave like old school Salubri. It doesn't fit how they are actually intended to behave.</div> </div> </div> </div>the same could be said of the animal feature by frenzy system,<br /> they need high humanity to keep self-control high enough to prevent frenzy and animal features<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whereas the animal feature flaw pushes them towards encouraging things to remain rural </div> </div> </div>in the Gangrel's case, what pushes stereotype is their discipline spread that is geared towards rural life,<br /> they don't have social disciplines like toreador or brujah that would favour a city life","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:25:39-07:00","id":1412048,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel weakness as-is (V20) is fine. It could use more guidelines (stop trying to be that animal you like so much, Alex. You're not a wolf Alex, you're not a crow, only you find this shit cool) (storyteller, don't give Alex a cow face, he deserves it, yeah, but the Beast should be picking from non-domesticated predators, parasites and scavengers here. You're punishing everybody by using farm animals...) <br /> I also feel the 'permanent' features should really just last a long time. <br /> <br /> I feel City Gangrel, having obfuscate, should have more severe curse-of-ugly mutations. All that said, I think both the clan disciplines and weakness of the clan are both really good for characters that both embrace and reject humanity. The important thing is that Gangrel are rugged individuals that can adapt, be self sufficient (or at least keep humans out of the pipeline; Animal help is great)<br /> <br /> For this reason, while I find Gangrel cool, I don't feel like i'm playing Vampire with them so much. I like having lots of humans around, they keep things interesting. A Gangrel is by nature much less invested in things, and I want to get invested in things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:34:45-07:00","id":1412049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412048#post1412048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For this reason, while I find Gangrel cool, I don't feel like i'm playing Vampire with them so much. I like having lots of humans around, they keep things interesting. A Gangrel is by nature much less invested in things, and I want to get invested in things.</div> </div> </div> </div>well they do get involved with fringe nomadic groups like romani communities or tribals,<br /> nowadays, it's easy to find outcasts, animal lovers, nature lovers, new age sects, eco-terrorists or activists that could share a gangrel's wild domain<br /> <br /> the only issue with that is that Lupines already occupy that space, and don't leave much to the Gangrel<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:53:00-07:00","id":1412052,"title":"","content":"lupines are few. I think there's stuff Gangrel can use that lupines wouldn't touch, like America's militia. if they can keep their weakness in check there is plenty they can do with mundane social skills or some small investments in OoC disciplines, but everyone can achieve this if they work at it. It's just more of a struggle. <br /> Squishy malkavians can also become physically mighty and the nosferatu can become social gods. It's just more work. The Gangrel are just more famous for being anti-social. And If you were seriously threatening a Gangrel's stuff, It'd be more willing to cut losses and run than a ventrue. Because the gangrel is more able to, and because the gangrel has more trouble keeping such attachments.<br /> edit:<br /> I suppose on the flipside may feel more invested in the connections made. But still they expect loneliness as the default state of unlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-05-2020, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:18:44-07:00","id":1412063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412041#post1412041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Toreador weakness pushes them towards encouraging art, because their disciplines are strongest when surrounded by beauty.</div> </div> </div> </div>... aren't they most VULNERABLE when surrounded by beauty? It's not unlike someone prone to getting hypnotised hanging up swirly spirals all over their apartment. By that logic, they should strive to keep everything bland and uninspired (could be an interesting approach); they encourage art and beauty because experiencing those things is addictive to them, or rather their Beast, much like the Ravnos' Beast is addicted to crime/sin.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:38:27-07:00","id":1412066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412063#post1412063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... aren't they most VULNERABLE when surrounded by beauty? It's not unlike someone prone to getting hypnotised hanging up swirly spirals all over their apartment. By that logic, they should strive to keep everything bland and uninspired (could be an interesting approach); they encourage art and beauty because experiencing those things is addictive to them, or rather their Beast, much like the Ravnos' Beast is addicted to crime/sin.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>no, when they're surrounded by bland things, they get more sensitive to beauty, so almost anything could transfix them<br /> <br /> however, if they're used to seeing beautiful things, they get bored and it gets harder to impress them and transfix them with the stuff they're used to seeing<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T08:47:33-07:00","id":1412098,"title":"","content":"Never thought of it that way. Thanks for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T10:05:40-07:00","id":1412109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412013#post1412013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every character should be self sufficient in night to night feeding. The Salubri and Capadocians got wiped so easily because their numbers were limited because their disciplines weren't great for feeding. The Nosferatu have three wonderful disciplines to make up for the ugly and the Samedi at least have the best discipline for it. By contrast the Toreador are the successful generalists of the kindred world that have all the powers they need to thrive anywhere civilisation can be found. Kiasyd pose too many challenges.A hoody, sunglasses and dodgy makeup is only going to attract more attention to the guy who look like he had surgery to become an eldari. If they had two dots of obfuscate, It'd be ok, but they don't. Their tranformation is just too extreme for Kiasyd.<br /> <br /> Maeghar... They're not so much of a problem.<br /> <br /> I want my players to play viable characters in a solo session, even if we're in a group. I want players to play believable characters, not something that only exists to fill a niche in the party and has to rely on everyone else for all the normal stuff. A good character shouldn't come from a vacuum to exist only when the party gets together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I had thought a UFO cult would make for an awesome herd for this sort of character, supplemented with dominate to get blood from outside sources. In modern nights with the internet, it's easier than ever to find dupes who'd think you're an alien. Ya you'd look sketchy in the makeup, but no worse than some humans look. A couple ghouls can really help to be the face to lure people in. They could trade occult favors and knowledge for boons to get other things they want. They can get by on their own, but it's easier to trade favors, which also makes them seem useful to the other vampires around the city. Even the Toreador, who are generalists tend to trade favors to get things that they're not good at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:02:48-07:00","id":1412117,"title":"","content":"People into UFO's are going to want to take pictures, kidnap you and start careers from your corpse; at the very least they'd be telling all their friends. They're an unpredictable lot and I don't think a Kiasyd would be safe with such a following. If the Kiasyd bloodline was formed from this behaviour, UFO obsession would need to have lasted longer, and they'd probably develop presence.. It'd be cool for a character, but dangerous, and also it doesn't leave you with a lot of legroom if you're a secretive alien who has entrusted a populace to keep your secret and yet you go outside to feed from new people and get caught you're going to betray the trust of your believers and... <br /> <br /> It can work, but it's really, really messy. You need some Get-out-of-jail cards if you're gonna do that sorta thing, and it kinda only works as a one-off rather than a bloodline thing. The bloodline is too old. The bloodline as written has a culture that would shun that kind of thing. Some Cainites might just kill you for a percieved masquerade violation (if they're not just trying to kill you for being an abomination)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:30:52-07:00","id":1412123,"title":"","content":"kiasyd is what happens when devs take the piss with sabbat bloodlines,<br /> it was an idea that should have died with 2e, but Revised doubled down on it by adding even more freakish bloodlines (looking at you, Harbingers of skulls)<br /> <br /> as far as &quot;kiasyd working as a bloodline&quot; goes, they're not any worse than the Tzimisce...but only in the sabbat, where that sort of blatant freakishness is normal<br /> <br /> but, the devs wasted too many pages on these freakish bloodlines, pages that could have been better used eplaining and detailing how sabbat logistics worked when it came to the blatant freakishness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:47:24-07:00","id":1412125,"title":"","content":"The Tzmisce, with vicissitude, are a perfectly functional clan. They might do things that have you question such, but on the whole they work: A non-restictive weakness when it comes to food types, Animalism is a good discipline for night-to night living, Auspex is a great discipline, Vicissitude used properly is a great discipline for living a full unlife; they can be beautiful for easy feeding, change their appearance for their safety, it can be weaponized in emergency, it can be used upon others to gain good allies, bloodform is just super convenient... Without Vicissitude they're very functional discount-Ventrue.<br /> <br /> The Kiasyd just don't function.<br /> The Harbringers of skulls are also shit, in that they have the curse of ugly but don't have obfuscate. But they're saved by the fact that they're exclusively elders and used to be something else when they were neonates.<br /> Blood brothers totally work. They're freakish but there's nothing problematic about their function. <br /> <br /> Most other bloodlines function pretty well. Gargoyles are questionable on their own but work well as dependents. I feel some bloodlines (Capadocians and Salubri) have limited themselves very badly (which is why they got eaten) but they're still functional as small clans/bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:18:55-07:00","id":1412133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412125#post1412125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzmisce, with vicissitude, are a perfectly functional clan. They might do things that have you question such, but on the whole they work: A non-restictive weakness when it comes to food types, Animalism is a good discipline for night-to night living, Auspex is a great discipline, Vicissitude used properly is a great discipline for living a full unlife; they can be beautiful for easy feeding, change their appearance for their safety, it can be weaponized in emergency, it can be used upon others to gain good allies, bloodform is just super convenient... Without Vicissitude they're very functional discount-Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, their mechanics work<br /> <br /> what doesn't work is their write-ups in the sabbat,<br /> the tzimisce aren't exactly the most masquerade friendly clan,<br /> they often twist their childe's face after embrace, and since the childe usually has low stats, they don't have the necessary skill to fix it,<br /> they use vicissitude to twist their enemies and leave them crawling in the streets,<br /> they often take on alien looks, which they can't revert back to normal instantly (unless they have celerity for a combination discipline which, in canon, they usually don't have),<br /> <br /> a tzimisce with vicissitude 5 or blood magic acting like this is fairly easy to justify, just as a Kiasyd with obtenebration 5 is,<br /> but not a starting one<br /> <br /> the same goes for sabbat nosferatu and salubri who, canonically, flash their freakish features,<br /> kiasyd aren't any worse than them<br /> <br /> this is why I added that last sentence:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but, the devs wasted too many pages on these freakish bloodlines, pages that could have been better used eplaining and detailing how sabbat logistics worked when it came to the blatant freakishness </div> </div> </div>and since there hasn't been a sabbat guide in like 20 years, it's unlikely we'll ever get a proper answer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:40:54-07:00","id":1412141,"title":"","content":"I just imagine such reports are exaggerated/a result of sabbat shitting in camarilla territory/propaganda<br /> <br /> Most Tzmisce would get wrecked in a monomancy. I imagine most packs would tell their fiend to wind their neck in and stop with the crazy shit. Fiend Neonates trying to imitate their elders and crafting themselves way above their skill level into demons and whatnot are going to be shunned. Your demon clown neonate fiend is a liability for the whole pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:55:21-07:00","id":1412144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412141#post1412141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just imagine such reports are exaggerated/a result of sabbat shitting in camarilla territory/propaganda</div> </div> </div> </div>nope, it's canon...well, Revised canon,<br /> I'm not sure where v20 stands on the issue, but they did nerf blood magic, so it's even harder to justify sabbat behavior<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Tzmisce would get wrecked in a monomancy. I imagine most packs would tell their fiend to wind their neck in and stop with the crazy shit. </div> </div> </div>that's social suicide, even bishops can't admit openly that they're upholding any semblance of masquerade (except the bishops that are elected for that specific purpose),<br /> and you certainly can't tell other sabbat to tone the shit down,<br /> <br /> and it's hard to tell a tzimisce to tone it down after the toreador rammed a guy's face into a car and the brujah threw the car into the nearest shop because of their clan weakness and the pack had to run from law enforcement as a result","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-05-2020, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:11:14-07:00","id":1412149,"title":"","content":"Sabbat packs that last usually only shit in someone else's yard. But even in the suicidal packs, you're not going to want to be close to the guy who walks around looking like the xenomorph's child from hell. He/She's a risk. You don't want to share a haven with them, you don't even want to meet up with them. Someone follows them, someone follows you. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat might flout the masquerade, but you can do that without winning the Darwin award. There's a difference between 'This one time I made myself a demon and raped a nun' and 'I walk around busy streets raping nuns and looking like a demon and I fleshcraft my name onto anyone I get my hands on'. <br /> <br /> People might play chicken (A game where you stand in front of oncomming cars and escape at the last possible moment or cause the car to change course), they still don't cross busy motorways like it's nomal. The Sabbat attitude to the Masquerade is exactly that. It's not social suicide to tell someone to stop being a literal dickhead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:30:12-07:00","id":1412155,"title":"","content":"Has anyone here ever done anything with the Daughters, incidentally? They seem terribly redundant with the Toreador about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:51:52-07:00","id":1412159,"title":"","content":"The Daughters are a bloodline of &quot;Whut? Why?&quot; <br /> <br /> They're mysterious (but there doesn't seem much going on with that mystery) they're exclusive (and it's a dumb exclusion) and they play like a malkavian/ventrue hybrid who embraces toreador culture insofar as they're all singers which somehow makes them both generic as vampires and... <i>one note </i>as characters. <br /> <br /> I think I put one into my game as a Bahari cult leader but she might as well've been one of the other three clans mentioned. They really don't have much story potential beyond -singer makes people mad, stop the singer- or as generic vampires. The clan weakness is a quirk at best. They're the Opposite of Kiasyd; They function (justification for female only bloodline: An elder hears the song of the DoC and hunts down male voices, which would be a cool story if only it wasn't so... couldn't anyone do this?) but you can't really have so much fun with a strange quest for them beyond what I just mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T15:58:26-07:00","id":1412177,"title":"","content":"Many of the bloodlines seemed to exist as greater setting mysteries to be explored and resolved. They really weren't meant to be as characters, but a plot device. But whether there actually was a greater mystery to be resolved (or it was simply JJ Abrams style Mystery Box hack BS) became irrelevant when their creators moved on, and the new developers and writers dropped it because of lack of interest and moved on to other things.<br /> <br /> When I ST my own games, my own rule is to never bring in vampires of a bloodline unless I have a specific plot in mind that requires them (as opposed that I could use any other vampires to do the same). So I've never used those bloodlines at all. <br /> <br /> Exception to those bloodlines that are just clans whose antedeluvians were slain since I consider them to simply to be members of the original clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:07:36-07:00","id":1412208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412117#post1412117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People into UFO's are going to want to take pictures, kidnap you and start careers from your corpse; at the very least they'd be telling all their friends. They're an unpredictable lot and I don't think a Kiasyd would be safe with such a following. If the Kiasyd bloodline was formed from this behaviour, UFO obsession would need to have lasted longer, and they'd probably develop presence.. It'd be cool for a character, but dangerous, and also it doesn't leave you with a lot of legroom if you're a secretive alien who has entrusted a populace to keep your secret and yet you go outside to feed from new people and get caught you're going to betray the trust of your believers and...<br /> <br /> It can work, but it's really, really messy. You need some Get-out-of-jail cards if you're gonna do that sorta thing, and it kinda only works as a one-off rather than a bloodline thing. The bloodline is too old. The bloodline as written has a culture that would shun that kind of thing. Some Cainites might just kill you for a percieved masquerade violation (if they're not just trying to kill you for being an abomination)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you've got to do it right like a proper mystery cult and have levels of initiation. People join UFO cults without any real proof already. Only the inner circle would get to meet you and access to you is restricted only to those who can be trusted not to tell anyone and have passed enough initiation tests and are either blood bound or dominated into loyalty. You could have some lies about needing them to donate blood so the aliens can help elevate humanity without ever needing to come into direct contact with the majority of the cult. I'm not saying this is how they all do things, just how I'd do it if I played one. Don't get me wrong, this is definitely not the type of character that would be a good fit for most chronicles. I just think it could be a fun way to play one and it'd interesting. Some of the example characters in Lore of the Bloodlines give some examples, like an Elysium mixologist that provides ways they've managed to survive. Most of the Sabbat ones probably work mainly as researchers in the background and are less active than say Nathaniel McCabe.<br /> <br /> I also personally like some of the weirder bloodlines, but I can see where some of you are coming from on feature creep. I do also realize they're more generally supposed to be used for ST characters and not generally playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T23:53:26-07:00","id":1412226,"title":"","content":"An categorization of bloodline viability: <br /> <br /> <b>Good and very playable: </b><br /> Most variations on a clan (antitribue, castes, laibon, Gangrel I don't mention elsewhere)<br /> Samedi<br /> Baali (assuming you don't play an evil infernalist)<br /> Warrior salubri<br /> <br /> <b>Good </b><br /> Baali (assuming you're playing an evil infernalist)<br /> Gargoyles<br /> Blood brothers<br /> Lamia<br /> The necromancers with the bad teeth I always forget the spelling of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Undecided/Complicated</b><br /> Capadocian; They do work but not well, especially in modern nights; they make a good cautionary tale and an example of a middling bloodline which would struggle to feed getting consumed by a better one with no such problem.<br /> Ahrimanes: They work in theory. I wasn't around for their metaplot.<br /> Witches of echidna: Mechanically, they're bad but workable. Fluff wise (at face value) they're bullshit. On the plus side I would be delighted to kill them for the glory of Set (assuming they don't starve to death first)<br /> <br /> <b>Meh/needs a little work</b><br /> DoC<br /> HoS<br /> Healer Salubri<br /> Anda (I still don't get why they have a full page for themselves in v20)<br /> Noiad<br /> Liahn<br /> Maeghar<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bullshit:</b><br /> Kiasyd.<br /> True Brujah (for Temporis alone, if it were just celerity they'd be good) (I forget they're supposed to exist untill something reminds me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-06-2020, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T06:28:50-07:00","id":1412267,"title":"","content":"Agreed about the DoC, MWIS. And good write up there, too.<br /> <br /> Pleiades, that's an idea I never heard before, but it makes a lot of sense, so thank you for sharing that.<br /> <br /> Heh. You know, the first time I learned of Masquerade was back in school. I vividly remember writing up questionnaires, lists of disciplines and all that and went around interviewing all my (very few) friends to see on which Clans they'd land. So yeah, I was doing the personality quizzes before I had any idea what THOSE were. Just a funny anecdote I'd thought I'd share, maybe someone else did something like that too?<br /> <br /> Regarding Favourite Clans, there's also a category of Clans I feel like it's great they exist, but I wouldn't want to play one. Like Brujah, who often are written up as uncomplicated thugs, or Tremere who are barely vampire and ninety-percent wizard transplanted into modern nights, and yes, the Toreador. They cater to a different playstyle than I would like to have to do but there are a ton of people who love it, and to them, they work fantastically well. Which is wonderful.<br /> <br /> On the other end of that spectrum, it seems to me are the Gangrel. Perhaps for reasons outlined by MyWifeIsScary: bestial vampire is an interesting concept, but the way they're written they become animal hodgepodges rather than fearsome predators, and an opportunity for storytellers to permanently humiliate PCs too tempting to pass up for some. It's telling how powerful NPCs (like Odin and his childer) will simply ignore how that Clan actually works. The only Clan I've seen less played over the years are the Ravnos, leading me to wonder if their design failed to provide what people were looking for. At least the Ravnos had the excuse of most of them dying by writer fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26275,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","user":"Konigheim Horror","date":". 09-06-2020, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:06:27-07:00","id":1412274,"title":"","content":"Ravnos would be a great top-teir clan if they didn't have a stigma of -doesn't play well with others- and -originally-super-racist. <br /> <br /> Chimestry has a lot of grey areas too. otherwise solid disciplines and the V20 weakness is good (yeah it's abusable, but the storyteller can veto a problematic vice. It's harder to clamp down on a fishmalk.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T09:54:48-07:00","id":1412305,"title":"","content":"I also like the Malkavians, for the whole madness, outsider, and outcast aspect of theirs. It's telling that many Vampires don't exactly want to be on the same team as the Malkavians, but at the same time they don't want the Malkavians to be on the opposing team. Also, their Discipline spread (whether with Dementation or Dominate, though I prefer Dominate) is really sweet - they are the only Clan with no physical Discipline. (there are also Tzimisce and Setites, but Vissicitude and Serpentis are inclined towards the physical, as opposed to the clearly otherworldly Disciplines of the Malkavians) The Malkavians' Disciplines lend so well to a trickster, spy, or scout (during wartime) archetype.<br /> <br /> There are also the True Brujah. Somehow their Discipline spread of Presence, Temporis, Potence seems to be the most vampiric to me. Covers a lot of bases - social attunement, temporal might, and otherworldly powers. It is nice that Temporis is said to flow from the very nature of Vampires as undead. I also like the fact that their Weakness can easily be interpreted as not a weakness at all, but a blessing. Aren't they freed from the burden of emotions, having a clear state of thoughts no matter the circumstances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-06-2020, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T11:56:16-07:00","id":1412321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412267#post1412267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's telling how powerful NPCs (like Odin and his childer) will simply ignore how that Clan actually works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Gangrel NPCs are a prominent example of writers not taking the rules seriously. Surely many old Gangrel (andeven some newly made) should have experienced frenzies and thus show some prominent bestial traits. At least some prominent ones should be mentioned in their description. There have been a few NPCs where this has been highlighted - Echidna and Canis come to mind - but overall, their weakness is seen as something of an obstacle the writers don't want to deal with and thus often ignored. In Werewolf, the Curse and the effects of Rage is another thing many writers ignore.<br /> <br /> In contrast, every gaming group I've seen has treated the Gangrel weakness seriously - probably because everyone is intensely aware of their own clan's specific weakness and expect to see it played out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T13:20:48-07:00","id":1412326,"title":"","content":"There used to be a high-level Fortitude power that just noped the Gangrel clan curse. It was why there was many elders that just don't show ay signs of it. Nosferatu that learned it died messily. Leading to some speculation as to why the Gangrel curse doesn't seem to stick as hard as some of the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T17:55:26-07:00","id":1412359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411232-favorite-clans-and-why?p=1412321#post1412321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many Gangrel NPCs are a prominent example of writers not taking the rules seriously. Surely many old Gangrel (andeven some newly made) should have experienced frenzies and thus show some prominent bestial traits. At least some prominent ones should be mentioned in their description. There have been a few NPCs where this has been highlighted - Echidna and Canis come to mind - but overall, their weakness is seen as something of an obstacle the writers don't want to deal with and thus often ignored. In Werewolf, the Curse and the effects of Rage is another thing many writers ignore.<br /> <br /> In contrast, every gaming group I've seen has treated the Gangrel weakness seriously - probably because everyone is intensely aware of their own clan's specific weakness and expect to see it played out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Made even worse by how the few &quot;animalistic&quot; features such Gangrel show (long hair and nails, feral expressions etc.) is something ANY vampire falling below the Humanity threshold could have. Low Humanity vampires are supposed to be low-key corpselike and unsettling to mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T18:02:02-07:00","id":1412362,"title":"","content":"My fav Clans are the ones that go full posthuman (like the Tzmiche, Gangrel, Lasombra, Setties, Gargoyals etc) and the ones with prominate pre-christian cultures (some of the previous but also Lhinnian, Dark Ages Ahrimanes, Anda ect). My fav Sect is the V20 Tal'Mehe'Ra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T01:51:39-07:00","id":1412697,"title":"","content":"I have to say Kiasyd. I'm a sucker for Fae/Changeling WoD so any chance to have a connection with that is a great thing. They also have my favorite discipline set, as anyone with necromancy mytherceria and obtenebration is terrifying to most kindre-... well most anything.You can summon/command wraiths and use all the broken necromancy powers. Become a hentai death machine with little trouble. AND use mytherceria to shut down any combat. Period. Or you could use it IN combat to have them ponder the riddle while you kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}